namespace pdg { /**
\fn pdg::Port::setClipRect(Rect inClipRect)
\brief Replace the single clipping rectangle for all drawing operations.

Coordinates are in Port pixels, independent of drawing transforms. The rectangle
is intersected with getDrawingArea(). Empty or fully offscreen rectangles suppress
all drawing. A later setClipRect() replaces this rectangle; there is no clip stack.
Fractional boundaries select pixel centers within the half-open rectangle.

\param inClipRect Axis-aligned drawing boundary, including an empty rectangle.
\return This Port, for chaining.
\see getClipRect(), resetClipRect(), Attributes::clipOverflow()
**/ }
